{% from 'networkpolicy.yml.j2' import networkpolicy with context %}
---
# sonarr and radarr reach this pod as the download client at `wireguard:8080` — a compat Service
# (service-wireguard.yaml.j2) that selects `app: qbittorrent`, carrying the hostname their SQLite
# databases hold. The Service name differs; the pod is the same, so a podSelector on
# `app: qbittorrent` covers it. The PORT is the WebUI port, which the macro call below passes
# explicitly; it equals the entry's `port`, and test_netpol_from.py fails if the two diverge.
#
# This rule is PORT-SCOPED: the baseline admits none of sonarr, radarr, qbittorrent-reach-probe,
# qbittorrent-prefs-check or homepage, so they reach this pod only through this rule and only on
# the WebUI port.
#
# TRAEFIK IS LISTED DELIBERATELY — do not remove it as redundant. While qbittorrent carries the
# baseline label the union is the same with or without it. The entry matters for a pod that
# lacks the label, which this policy alone selects, and it keeps this policy's caller set
# complete if the baseline's traefik rule is ever port-scoped.
#
# qbittorrent-reach-probe (the `qbittorrent-verify` Job, templates/verify/job.yaml.j2) is
# load-bearing: it proves qbittorrent is reachable from the POD CIDR specifically, despite the
# Mullvad kill-switch's iptables rules on the wireguard sidecar. Fence that probe out and the check
# would pass-or-fail on this policy alone, silently inverting what it asserts: the one regression
# it exists to catch (the kill-switch swallowing pod-CIDR traffic) would read as green. Same shape
# as k8s/roles/registry/templates/networkpolicy.yaml.j2 admitting its own selftest Jobs. The Job's
# pod carries this app label; the template's DECIDED note says why.
#
# homepage's widget authenticates to the WebUI over the ClusterIP, not through Traefik, because
# qbittorrent's public route is Authelia-gated; fencing it out breaks the widget.
#
# qbittorrent-prefs-check is the daily drift check's CronJob (prefs-check-cronjob.yaml.j2). It
# dials the WebUI Service directly, so this entry is its whole grant. It lands in the same apply
# as the CronJob, because this role renders the fence.
#
# The caller list is `netpol_from:` on this role's containers_list entry (cluster/services.yml),
# each caller's reason beside it. `homepage_widget: true` adds homepage through the
# `netpol_callers` filter, and `netpol_role_owned: true` keeps netpol-baseline from
# rendering a second copy.
{{ networkpolicy(container_item.name, qbittorrent_k8s_webui_port, container_item | netpol_callers) }}
